- Fix: a query that fails before sending any data on an FDA with a download policy (cached or only-fresh) no longer consumes a download; downloads interrupted mid-stream still count (#375)
- Fix: a fresh NDJSON/CSV query that fails in PostgreSQL no longer hangs the request or leaks its pool connection (#386)
- Add: SQL output (`outputType=sql` / `Accept: application/sql`) for only-fresh PostgreSQL FDAs: a pg_dump-like script, as INSERT or COPY, that recreates the result as a table (optionally a TimescaleDB hypertable) in one transaction (#387)
- Add: support DateTime values in DA param range, with ISO 8601 bounds (#389)
